// Title: a select guard needs whitespace on both sides of `if`, so
// `n if(n > 1)` and `(a, b)if a > b` are refused, although `select(x)`
// takes its keyword followed directly by a bracket.
// Command: /home/eric/tmp/review-2026-10-26/bin/graphix --check design/review-2026-10-26/repro/t-parser-b-guard-if-paren.gx
// Expected: check passes (the guard keyword ends at a non-identifier char).
// Observed: Parse error at line 8, column 31: "Unexpected `i`, Expected
//   whitespace or =>", the caret on `if`.
let f = |x: i64| select x { n if(n > 1) => 1, _ => 2 };
f(3)
